    items:
      - title: What is an Enterprise Data Core?
        content: It is a unified, structured representation of your business. It organizes your data around real business events and entities, creating a single, trusted logic layer for all reporting, analytics, and AI.
      - title: How is it different from a data warehouse?
        content: A data warehouse stores and integrates raw data. An Enterprise Data Core adds standardized business context, metrics, and rules. This ensures everyone queries the same defined logic rather than writing their own rules in separate tools.
      - title: How does it support AI?
        content: AI is only as good as the context it is given. By standardizing your business entities and metrics, the Enterprise Data Core provides AI models with clean, structured, and explainable data, drastically reducing errors and manual validation.
      - title: Why do you use dimensional modeling?
        content: Dimensional modeling provides a simple, scalable way to represent how a business operates. Organizing data around business events (facts) and business entities (dimensions), it creates models that are intuitive, performant, and easy to use for reporting, analytics, and AI.
      - title: Can you combine data from multiple systems?
        content: Yes. We integrate data from ERP, CRM, EPM, operational systems, and third-party applications into a single, consistent business model, enabling analysis across systems rather than within individual applications.
      - title: Is the Enterprise Data Core only for reporting?
        content: No. While it improves reporting and analytics, it also provides the trusted, governed context needed for AI, automation, planning, and operational applications.
